WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.734
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:05.300
You're here. You made it. Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:10.334
Thank you for being here. Let's get to some news.

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:13.067
Guys, today the Bidens hosted the Obamas

00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:16.167
for the unveiling of their White House portraits.

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:18.734
Yeah, the unveiling of the portraits took so long

00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:20.300
because they spent the last six months

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.934
in the basement of Mar-a-lago.

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:24.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:29.167
That's right -- the Obamas were at the White House

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:31.801
for the portrait unveiling, and it's a little different

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:34.234
than I thought it would be. Watch this.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.601
-All set? Here we go.

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:38.667
[ Audience oohs ]

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:40.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:44.834 --> 00:00:46.767
-That's the one they went with.

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:48.334
-Goodness! -Yeah.

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:50.868
-Can we see the actual portraits?

00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:52.467
This is real. These are real.

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:54.567
Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:57.033
To sum it up, she looks like American royalty.

00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:58.834
He looks like he's looking for a job on LinkedIn.

00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:00.701
Can we -- Can we see that portrait?

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:02.200
Look at -- Look at Barack's portrait.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:06.033
It looks like he's about to introduce the new iPhone.

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:10.868
He's like -- [as Obama] "I'm a Mac and he's a PC."

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:14.067
"48 megapixel."

00:01:14.067 --> 00:01:16.100
[Normal voice] Barack was like, "Give me something that could

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.567
double as a passport photo, if you don't mind."

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:19.801
I mean, come on.

00:01:19.801 --> 00:01:21.634
Even the school-picture laser background

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:24.834
would have been better than what -- Come on.

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:27.067
That's what he should have gone with.

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:29.000
Well, get this. According to a new book,

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Trump once owed a lawyer $2 million,

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.300
and he tried to pay with the deed to a horse.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.200
That's how crazy Trump's life is.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.567
There are 100 tell-all books,

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:41.534
and somehow there's still more to tell.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:44.400
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.100
Speaking of trump, I read that when

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.567
the FBI searched Mar-a-lago,

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:49.634
they seized material that had information

00:01:49.634 --> 00:01:53.067
on a foreign country's nuclear capabilities.

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:55.300
After the news broke, a Fox News host suggested

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:58.968
that Trump might have been trying to sell the information.

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:00.501
Trump was like, "Hypothetically,

00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:02.634
how many horses do you think that would be worth?"

00:02:02.634 --> 00:02:06.300
[ Laughter ] "Two horses?"

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.968
A lot of people are talking about this.

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:10.000
Tomorrow, former Trump aide Steve Bannon,

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.601
who is apparently facing a new criminal indictment,

00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:16.334
is expected to turn himself in to New York state prosecutors.

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:18.801
Yeah. Can we see Steve Bannon again?

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:21.000
Yeah, that -- that --

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.801
that's what he looks like before prison.

00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:24.400
Uh, it's interesting.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.400
Some tech news.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.033
Today Apple launched the iPhone 14,

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:31.534
and the early reviews on it are fantastic.

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:33.400
Apparently it got an 8-minute standing ovation

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.834
at the Venice Film Festival.

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:37.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:41.968
-Come on! Come on!

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:43.434
-Eight minutes. Unbelievable.

00:02:43.434 --> 00:02:45.400
-Come on. Eight-minute standing ovation.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.634
For an iPhone! -At the Venice Film Festival.

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:50.133
Oh, my gosh.

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:51.334
The new iPhone --

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:52.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:54.901
-Come on. That's a good joke. -Can you believe it? Yeah.

00:02:54.901 --> 00:02:57.033
The new iPhone -- -Come on, people.

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:59.334
-The new iPhone Pro comes in four new colors.

00:02:59.334 --> 00:03:01.868
Here are the colors. Yeah, ooh. -Oh, wow.

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:05.934
-The new colors are Darth Vader, R2-D2, C-3PO...

00:03:05.934 --> 00:03:07.868
and Tinky Winky.

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:10.934
Uh -- Very -- It's fascinating.

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:13.834
That's right. Apple unveiled the new iPhone 14 today.

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:15.467
-I don't know what everyone just uses

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:17.434
the same type of phone for.

00:03:17.434 --> 00:03:19.501
-What do you mean? What kind of phone do you have?

00:03:19.501 --> 00:03:22.000
-It's a, you know, an Enron T-Minus-Plus.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.934
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:23.934 --> 00:03:25.367
-I thought -- I thought --

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:27.067
I thought Enron didn't exist anymore.

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:28.501
-They're b-a-a-ack.

00:03:28.501 --> 00:03:31.267
And they make phones now.

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:33.234
Like, anything you can do on an iPhone,

00:03:33.234 --> 00:03:34.567
I can do on this thing.

00:03:34.567 --> 00:03:38.200
Except text. Or go on the Internet.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.200
-Wait. It can't even text? -Don't need to, Jimmy.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.901
Not when you got an amazing service like I do.

00:03:43.901 --> 00:03:47.300
The Enron T-Minus-Plus has 1G technology.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.834
-It has 1G? My phone has 5G.

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:51.734
-1G is just like 5G,

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:54.634
except I only get reception when I'm in an open field

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.300
or near a very powerful microwave.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:57.767
-Yeah, I think I'm gonna have to

00:03:57.767 --> 00:03:59.601
just stick with the phone that I have.

00:03:59.601 --> 00:04:01.033
Thank you, though. -Your loss.

00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:03.267
The Enron T-Minus-Plus

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:06.534
even has a virtual assistant, just like Siri.

00:04:06.534 --> 00:04:08.501
His name is Ritchie.

00:04:08.501 --> 00:04:10.167
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:12.100
Hey, Ritchie, can you --

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.267
can you tell me the capital of Belgium?

00:04:14.267 --> 00:04:16.901
-I'm tired!

00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:18.100
-I -- I -- I don't know.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.067
That doesn't seem like a great phone to me.

00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:21.434
-Up yours, Jimmy!

00:04:21.434 --> 00:04:24.601
-Ha ha! This phone's the best.

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:27.234
Ritchie, you're funny, man!

00:04:27.234 --> 00:04:29.367
-I'm tired! -Alright, Tariq

00:04:29.367 --> 00:04:31.634
and the Enron T-Minus-Plus, everyone.

00:04:31.634 --> 00:04:33.701
I don't know... -I'm tired!

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:35.434
-I know. I heard, "I'm tired." Yeah.

00:04:35.434 --> 00:04:37.400
[ Applause ]

00:04:39.801 --> 00:04:40.934
Guys, listen to this.

00:04:40.934 --> 00:04:42.267
Juul has agreed to pay

00:04:42.267 --> 00:04:45.100
over $400 million to settle a lawsuit.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.501
Juul, the -- Not the singer.

00:04:47.501 --> 00:04:50.033
I'm talking about the e-cigarette, yeah, sorry.

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:52.033
$400 million to settle a lawsuit that they were

00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:55.100
illegally marketing vaping products to children.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.434
[ Audience ohhs ] Yeah, that's not allowed, no.

00:04:57.434 --> 00:04:59.801
But I think they're still trying to get kids to buy Juuls.

00:04:59.801 --> 00:05:02.400
It's odd. Check out this product placement I saw the other day.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.834
-Will you check my backpack

00:05:03.834 --> 00:05:06.968
for something that can shine light into the cave?

00:05:06.968 --> 00:05:09.901
-A rubber duck? A flashlight?

00:05:09.901 --> 00:05:13.000
A refreshing mint Juul?

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.634
Did you say, "Refreshing mint Juul"?

00:05:16.634 --> 00:05:18.033
Muy bien!

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:19.634
-Yeah, no. You see what I'm saying?

00:05:19.634 --> 00:05:21.100
That's not one of the...

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:22.968
[ Applause ]

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:25.968
-That didn't seem right. -No.

00:05:25.968 --> 00:05:27.501
Well, some news from overseas.

00:05:27.501 --> 00:05:29.868
According to a new report, Russia is now buying

00:05:29.868 --> 00:05:31.734
military supplies from North Korea.

00:05:31.734 --> 00:05:32.968
-Ooh.

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:35.334
Yeah, Russia is asking North Korea for help.

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:36.667
Tell us you're losing the war

00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:38.667
without telling us you're losing the war.

00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:40.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.767 --> 00:05:42.934
Well, I saw that another cryptocurrency crash

00:05:42.934 --> 00:05:45.501
could be coming, and a lot of people are pretty worried.

00:05:45.501 --> 00:05:47.767
Well, luckily, there's a new product to help with that.

00:05:47.767 --> 00:05:49.067
Take a look at this commercial.

00:05:49.067 --> 00:05:51.300
-Are you suffering from heartburn, nausea,

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.667
and an upset stomach

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:55.501
all because you lost your life savings on crypto?

00:05:55.501 --> 00:05:57.834
Introducing Crypto-Bismol.

00:05:57.834 --> 00:06:00.534
-I was hit hard by the recent crypto crash.

00:06:00.534 --> 00:06:02.300
I did everything you were supposed to do.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:03.767
I hired a great business manager.

00:06:03.767 --> 00:06:05.968
He's 15 years old and huge on "Fortnite."

00:06:05.968 --> 00:06:07.934
That's why I'm glad I take Crypto-Bismol.

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:10.734
-I poured all my money into something called Dank Coin.

00:06:10.734 --> 00:06:13.767
What is Dank Coin? I still don't know.

00:06:13.767 --> 00:06:16.534
That's why I use Crypto-Bismol!

00:06:16.534 --> 00:06:18.467
-Crypto-Bismol soothes your anxiety

00:06:18.467 --> 00:06:20.300
after you wasted your kid's college fund

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:23.267
on a JPEG of a zebra with a Mohawk and braces.

00:06:23.267 --> 00:06:24.934
Crypto-Bismol may be right for you

00:06:24.934 --> 00:06:26.601
if you suffer from any of the following

00:06:26.601 --> 00:06:28.767
crypto-related illnesses.

00:06:34.334 --> 00:06:37.467
-Thank you, Crypto-Bismol. I feel better already.

00:06:37.467 --> 00:06:40.267
-Crypto-Bismol. Now available as an NFT.

00:06:40.267 --> 00:06:41.901
-Yeah, that's interesting. Yeah.

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:44.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:48.901 --> 00:06:51.267
You guys see this? Today, after more than two years,

00:06:51.267 --> 00:06:54.300
New York lifted its mask mandate for the subway.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:56.667
-Ooh. -New Yorkers are like...

00:06:56.667 --> 00:06:59.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:59.067 --> 00:07:02.000
New Yorkers are like, "Yeah, I'm so happy they lifted

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:05.567
the mandate that I stopped following a year ago."

00:07:05.567 --> 00:07:07.934
Now the only thing covering your face in the subway

00:07:07.934 --> 00:07:10.801
will be the armpit of the guy standing next to you.

00:07:10.801 --> 00:07:14.167
"How you doing? You getting on this?"

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:16.167
Yep, you'll be able to see everyone's faces

00:07:16.167 --> 00:07:18.067
as they follow the single Snapple bottle

00:07:18.067 --> 00:07:21.334
that's been rolling under the seat since 1995.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:25.968
I hope that's iced tea. Yeah.

00:07:25.968 --> 00:07:27.968
[ Rim shot ]

00:07:27.968 --> 00:07:30.133
-Apple juice!

00:07:30.133 --> 00:07:31.667
-Guys, listen to this.

00:07:31.667 --> 00:07:34.567
New York City public schools just announced that from now on,

00:07:34.567 --> 00:07:37.267
snow days will be remote learning days.

00:07:37.267 --> 00:07:40.100
[ Audience boos ]

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:42.167
During the announcement, both kids and parents were like,

00:07:42.167 --> 00:07:45.167
"Wait. What?! Now -- What?!"

00:07:45.167 --> 00:07:48.167
Finally, I heard that in an effort to reduce waste

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:50.467
caused by plastic espresso capsules,

00:07:50.467 --> 00:07:53.734
a Swiss retailer is releasing an eco-friendly alternative

00:07:53.734 --> 00:07:55.567
called "Coffee Balls."

00:07:55.567 --> 00:07:58.067
-No. Ohh!

00:07:58.067 --> 00:08:00.334
-Coffee Balls. That sounds like something

00:08:00.334 --> 00:08:01.667
you'd sue McDonald's for.

00:08:01.667 --> 00:08:03.467
Uh...

00:08:03.467 --> 00:08:06.734
[ Laughter ]

00:08:06.734 --> 00:08:09.167
It probably explains this new mug I saw.

00:08:09.167 --> 00:08:11.033
"Don't talk to me til I've had my balls."

00:08:11.033 --> 00:08:13.834
There you go. We have -- We have a great show tonight.

00:08:13.834 --> 00:08:16.400
Susan Sarandon is here!

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.100
Julio Torres is on the show.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.901
And we've got music from Fletcher!

00:08:19.901 --> 00:08:21.634
Stick around. We'll be right back

00:08:21.634 --> 00:08:23.801
with "Battle of the Instant Songwriters."

